// four-up-dummy — a fold-test dummy for the four-up-booklet arrangement. Eight A6 pages, each a single big
// numeral, imposed four-up on one A4 sheet (two PDF pages: sheet front, sheet back). Print double-sided
// (long-edge binding), cut the A4 in half across the middle into two A5 sheets, fold each A5 down the middle,
// nest the top A5 around the bottom one, and the numerals should read 1..8 in order. If they don't, the printer's
// duplex flip is short-edge, not long-edge — switch the print setting and try again.

\geometry paper:a6 margin:12mm
\arrange four-up-booklet

\def num n {\vfil\hbox to:\hsize {\hss\font lmroman 140 regular \n\hss}\vfil\eject}

\num{1}
\num{2}
\num{3}
\num{4}
\num{5}
\num{6}
\num{7}
\num{8}
